  "Only one of these jumps survives.",
  "Pick one: a world to skydive into.",
  "Pick one, two, three or four, and comment. Think about it.",
  "One, Mars. The air is less than one percent as thick as Earth's.",
  "Even under its parachute, NASA's rover was still falling at two hundred miles an hour.",
  "Two, Venus. Below its acid clouds, the air pressure is ninety times Earth's.",
  "It's hot enough to melt lead. The toughest lander lasted about two hours.",
  "Three, Jupiter. There's no ground. You'd just keep falling into crushing heat.",
  "NASA's Galileo probe tried it in nineteen ninety five, and went silent after about an hour.",
  "Four, Titan. Thick air and tiny gravity mean you fall slowly.",
  "Its Huygens probe drifted down for nearly two and a half hours.",
  "Strap on wings, and scientists think you might even fly."
